      "description": "Circular rag weaving on a35½-inch hula hoop. Twenty-seven rag loops make54 spokes; at one edge, separate a doubled spoke to create the odd spoke count needed to spiral without reversing the over-under order. Work plain weave outward and use the published half-basketweave option by pairing neighboring spokes. This editable linear ground represents the interlacement; radial shaping, the odd spoke and final knots are manual.",
      "kind": "Ground draft",
      "manualTechnique": true,
      "groupId": "handwoven-2015-05-06"
