      "manualTechnique": "Starting from the right with the heddle down, stick A selects slot ends after 5 down, then 1 up/5 down across. For towel 2, stick B selects the remaining contrast ends:8 down, then 1 up/5 down, ending 1 up/8 down. Heddle-up plus the selected stick makes each warp-float pick. Towel 1 cycle: down, up+A, down, up, down, up, down, up. Towel 2 cycle: down, up+A, down, up, down, up, down, up+B, down, up, down, up. Use 1¾-inch plain-weave hems; body 26 inches for towel 1 or 25½ inches plus first 6 cycle steps for towel 2.",
