      "manualTechnique": "Weave 4 inches plain for the rod pocket. On an open shed, from the right pass under the first 7 raised ends; return around the preceding 6 raised ends, excluding the edge end. Continue in 6-raised-end bouquets (two ends of each color), advancing 12 and returning 6 each time. Make 18 bouquets, finish through the remaining 2 raised ends, change shed and weave 7 plain picks. Repeat across 39 inches of lace; finish with 2 inches plain for the hem.",
