      "designer": "Carol James",
      "description": "Eight-end hand fingerweaving in worsted yarn. This two-shed grid is a ground schematic only: each rightmost warp end becomes the next weft and returns at the opposite edge, so a fixed loom draft cannot reproduce the braid. The third color is an illustrative choice; the publication permits colors of choice.",
