      "manualTechnique": "Cut 4 yard-long strands and fold to 8 ends of 18 inches. Hold the cross with 2 sticks and tape to a table. Alternate upper/lower ends. Select the rightmost end and take it across the open shed as weft; return it at the left edge, exchange the upper/lower ends and repeat. Tighten by separating the two groups, then gently tug each end. Alternating variant starts turquoise at right. Diagonal variant groups 4 white and 4 turquoise. Three-color order is 1,2,2,1,3,3,3,3 from left to right; first 4 wefts use color 3, then 1,2,2,1.",
      "kind": "ground-draft",
      "groupId": "handwoven-2019-03-04"
