      "manualTechnique": "Choose random warp stripes at least 2 ends wide. Weave 1 inch(es) with Natural 8/2 for the first hem, then 16 inches with Natural bouclé. At irregular intervals lay short Black 8/4 cotton lengths in the same shed as the bouclé; vary their lengths and positions across the width. Finish with 1 inch(es) of 8/2. These partial-width inlays are hand placed and cannot be represented by a single whole-width weft color.",
